# Behavioural coverage row 12 "Multiple cities": found a second, independent city of the same realm
# on a NON-adjacent surface zone, one world parasang out and three zones from city one, refuse a
# further founding on ground now held, and prove the seat comes back on the return to city one.
#
# City one is founded by the built-in realize verb -- the production first-city transaction,
# never a harness copy -- and then lives one ordinary turn (advance 1). That turn is required:
# production's ZoneActivatedEvent handler seats a returning founder only after
# KingdomMaster.ObserveAutomaticWake, which consumes the wake on the tick the master latch
# changes (Core/KingdomMaster.cs). Without it, realize, the latch's first observation and both
# controlled transfers share one tick and the return leg would read a consumed wake. The setup
# verb re-proves the latch with KingdomMaster.AutomaticWorkAllowed; no case after it spends a
# turn. City two is founded through KingdomFoundingTransaction.TryFoundSecondWithoutWater -- the
# exact call KingdomFounding.FoundSecond (Core/KingdomFounding.03.SiteJudgmentAndStyle.cs)
# makes, taken directly so a refusal keeps its sentence -- with Force FALSE so the adjacency
# law stands.
#
# SYNTHETIC SETUP, DISCLOSED:
#  - the founder is relocated with zero-energy SystemMoveTo plus SetActiveZone, not walked
#    across the world map; travel time, encounters and the away economy are NOT exercised.
#  - the waterless route: the rite's 8-dram debit and its three Popup prompts (name, vocation,
#    refusal) are NOT exercised. A sealed script cannot answer a popup, and
#    Harness/KingdomScenarioVerbProvider.cs forbids a provider from showing one.
#  - the second site is ordinary worldgen; only the START zone is born-clean. Candidates
#    start one world parasang out, three zones from city one (production judges closeness per
#    zone), and at most 8 are built, nearest first: setup refuses unless the candidates built
#    are exactly the nearest ones in order, each rejected with a reason or chosen. A candidate
#    is accepted only if it builds, answers to no foreign faction and reads Allowed from
#    KingdomFounding.JudgeSite, which alone decides held and too-close ground, and only on an
#    empty rite cell, nearest city one's rite, whose rung-1 heart rect holds no liquid and
#    which passes production's own read-only founding-heart preflight
#    (KingdomArchitectureRuntime.TryPrepareFoundingHeart: the basin binds to the rite and the
#    authored entrance is walkable). Every rejected candidate is journalled with its reason in
#    the second-city-site row, whether a site qualifies or the search refuses (the row is then
#    REFUSED); each reason is kept to 512 characters there, with a marker naming any cut, and
#    goes uncut to Player.log.
#  - city two has no population, buildings, stockpile or economy, and no case spends a turn:
#    every case re-proves Game.Turns and Game.TimeTicks are unchanged since setup.
#
# NOT COVERED, DISCLOSED: save -> cold load -> next action on either city (row 12's
# save_cold_load sub-scope stays a gap), the third city and the RealmIsFull cap, and ordinary
# pedestrian travel between the two cities.
#
# The return leg asserts production's own seat exchange: KingdomSystem.HandleEvent
# (ZoneActivatedEvent) calls TrySeat before the claim guard (Core/KingdomSystem.z20.Events.cs),
# so activating the first city's ground must bring its seat back with nothing seated here.
# The same handler then runs the realm's FIRST polity reconciliation: founding stamps the
# semantic clock, so no settlement pass (and no daily reconciliation) is due in this one-turn
# run, travel-out's unclaimed ground leaves the handler before polity, and nothing loads.
# Setup proves no polity window is open; the return case requires production to have opened
# this period's window over both cities.
#
# FORBIDDEN DIAGNOSTICS: that handler only LOGS five refusals, no verb fails on them and
# Tools/check-player-log.sh passes them, so LOG_FORBID names all five in three literals: the
# founding-heart reserved-identity audit and the legacy plot-effect recovery (both run on
# every activation, so on travel-out and on the return before the seat moves), and
# "reconciliation refused", which covers the hosted authority and hosted interior activation
# refusals (every activation) and the polity zone reconciliation (the return, after the seat),
# and also every other reconciliation refusal production logs. The fourth literal is the
# attended settlement pass's founding-heart recovery refusal, which the camp-heart personas
# forbid too; no pass is due in this run, so it guards a pass that runs unexpectedly (that
# pass's seal-staging refusal does not fit the four-literal cap). A polity refusal on the
# return is the two-city realm's first reconciliation refusing: it is row-12 evidence, read
# by its logged reason, and not the earlier-window refusal tracked in #244 and #257.
DESCRIPTION=a realm founds a second city on a non-adjacent surface zone three zones from the first city, refuses a further founding on its own ground, and recovers the first city's seat on return
REQUEST=founding-first-city
START=8.22@40,12
SCRIPT=stagedigest;realize;advance 1;second-city-setup;second-city-check;second-city-check;second-city-check;second-city-check;stagedigest
VERBS=second-city-setup,second-city-check
EXPECT=stagedigest:OK~founded=false,realize:OK,advance:OK,second-city-site:OK~adjacent=false,second-city-setup:OK~cases=4 passed=0 failed=0,second-city-check:OK~case=travel-out,second-city-topology:OK~settlements=2,second-city-check:OK~case=found-second,second-city-check:OK~case=refused-already-ours,second-city-check:OK~cases=4 passed=4 failed=0,stagedigest:OK~founded=true,COMPLETE
SET=founding,growth,native-regression
LOG_FORBID=["founding heart: reserved identity audit refused","plot effects: active-zone legacy recovery refused","reconciliation refused","construction: founding heart recovery requires inspection"]
TIMEOUT=900
